Fix positional sounds silent: implement alDistanceModel() and default to
the linear distance model.

alDistanceModel() was a no-op that only set an error, so the distance model
stayed stuck at AL_INVERSE_DISTANCE_CLAMPED. With the inverse model a source
falls to near-silence within a few world units (gain = ref/(rolloff*dist)),
so positional sounds like projectile flight or bullet impacts are inaudible,
while sources attached to the listener (distance 0) stay full volume.

Quake-derived backends (e.g. makroncast) set REFERENCE_DISTANCE=1,
MAX_DISTANCE=8192 and ROLLOFF_FACTOR=dist_mult*8191 expecting
AL_LINEAR_DISTANCE_CLAMPED, which reproduces the engine's linear falloff
(1 - dist_mult*(dist-1)). Implement the API and default the model to
AL_LINEAR_DISTANCE_CLAMPED so those parameters work out of the box.
--- a/src/core.c
+++ b/src/core.c
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 #include "private.h"
 
 static ALenum CURRENT_ERROR = AL_NO_ERROR;
-static ALenum DISTANCE_MODEL = AL_INVERSE_DISTANCE_CLAMPED;
+static ALenum DISTANCE_MODEL = AL_LINEAR_DISTANCE_CLAMPED;
 
 ALboolean _alSetError(const char* func, ALenum error, const ALchar* msg) {
     if(CURRENT_ERROR == AL_NO_ERROR) {
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@
 }
 
 AL_API void AL_APIENTRY alDistanceModel(ALenum distanceModel) {
-    _alSetError(__func__, AL_INVALID_OPERATION, "Not Implemented");
+    DISTANCE_MODEL = distanceModel;
 }
 
 AL_API void AL_APIENTRY alEnable(ALenum capability) {
